{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"boundary","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A startup failure can remove the token-file read denial while integration workers are still stopping, leaving sandbox policies created during that interval without the intended protection."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Enabling token enforcement with an accepted plain-HTTP proxy configuration leaves the browser unable to maintain a session, making the remote UI inaccessible."}]}